>> I don't know how nethack handles the termcap delay code for OS/2.
>
> Without TIMED_DELAY there seems to be no delay at all.
> tty_delay_output in termcap.c has 'simulate the delay with "cursor here',
> but I guess that was calibrated with 386 processors in mind. For some
> reason this "delay" is used even when TIMED_DELAY is defined.

     When built with TIMED_DELAY enabled, run-time behavior is
controlled by an option (called `timed_delay').  And when that
option is enabled, the `flags.nap' part of tty_delay_output() is
used.  So the implementation of msleep() is relevant in that case
and the MICRO part of tty_delay_output() won't be reached.

     To set timed_delay in via NETHACKOPTIONS or config file,
you need to specify at least five characters of its name.  If you
use less, you'll just be manipulating the `time' setting on the
status line.


